tches, and industrial lasers, including short-pulse solid-state lasers and kilowatt-class fiber lasers. Its products and solutions are used in cloud, artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML), telecommunications, consumer, and industrial end-market applications. The company was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael E.  Hurlston | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $219K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 14\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Lumentum Holdings Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $54.1B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $300M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 448% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.480522220779857},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $41.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Lumentum Holdings (LITE) Following The Marvell Deal How Cheap Is The Stock","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-lite/lumentum-holdings/news/lumentum-holdings-lite-following-the-marvell-d